# Everything listed here is withheld from the Docker build context — the tarball
# the CLI ships to the daemon before a single instruction runs. The repo root is
# ~2.8 GB on disk and the API image needs maybe 2 MB of it, so this file is the
# difference between a build that takes seconds and one that takes minutes.
#
# Note this is a DENY list: anything not named here is sent. That direction is
# deliberate — the backend reaches the top-level analytics/, db.py, feeds.py,
# home_news/, technologies.py, toqan/ and vectordb/ modules transitively, and an
# allow list would silently drop one the next time an import is added.
#
# Comments must sit on their own line. Docker does not strip trailing comments,
# so `venv/  # big` would be read as a pattern that matches nothing.

# ── Secrets: never bake these into a layer ───────────────────────────────────
# Layers are cached, shipped and trivially unpacked (`docker history`), so a
# baked .env leaks to anyone who pulls the image. Compose injects it at RUN time
# instead, via `env_file` — see docker-compose.yml.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Heavy and irrelevant (the 2.8 GB) ────────────────────────────────────────
# 1.8 GB of private source material.
MOT project/
# 767 MB of macOS-built wheels; Linux rebuilds them from requirements.txt anyway.
venv/
.venv/
# 46 MB of history the runtime never reads.
.git/
# 19 MB, including screenshot evidence.
eval/
# 7 MB of marketing media.
linkedin-assets/
# This is the deployment image, not the CI image — Dockerfile.ci covers tests.
tests/
logo/
Skills/
SQL Tables/
Agents_prompt/
Pharos improvements/

# ── The frontend: built by its own image, from its own context ───────────────
# frontend/Dockerfile does the npm build. Sending 174 MB of node_modules into
# the API build would be pure waste.
frontend/
node_modules/

# ── Build/run detritus ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
logs/
*.log

# ── Docker's own files ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
